      <activity id="78316e72-d42e-5497-8586-f48760522868" activityNameId="082e3396-8fc9-5263-8520-cf0d6492ec6b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cantilever retaining wall, reinforced concrete, 1m, complete system</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cantilever retaining wall, reinforced concrete, 1m, complete system
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 3cb5b95c-8174-4dc8-b115-4a060de3ee34
This process models 1 meter cantilever retaining wall with a height of 5.4 meters. It includes the production phase (A1–A3), the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) as well as deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for one meter of cantiliever retaining wall.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: According to ASTRA (2025), project specific data related to study "Anwendung der Ökobilanz-Methode für die Infrastruktur von Nationalstrassen".
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3cb5b95c-8174-4dc8-b115-4a060de3ee34.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
